<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine weekly official crop progress.</title>
<headline>Argentine weekly official crop progress.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine farmers had sown 40.5 percent of their 1997/98 wheat crop by July 4, the Agriculture Secretariat said in its weekly report Thursday.</p>
<p>Farmers in almost all of Cordoba province and in the central and southern central areas of Santa Fe were having problems sowing due to drought. But excess moisture was delaying fieldwork in Buenos Aires, particularly in the western and central zones of the province. Sodden fields were also a problem in La Pampa. Farmers have mainly finished sowing longer-cycle wheat and are moving on to medium-cycle. Fertilizer use is down from last season.  </p>
<p>Intended total planting (thousands of hectares) and the percentage already sown (year-earlier in brackets). Harvest levels (thousands of hectares) and as a percentage of planted area, (year-earlier in brackets).</p>
<p> ..........Planting.............Harvest..............</p>
<p> Wheat     6,500  40.5  (63.9)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)</p>
<p> Maize     3,926  100.0(100.0) 3,102.6   96.3  (94.9)</p>
<p> Soybeans  6,648  100.0(100.0) 6,346.9   99.8 (100.0)</p>
<p> Sunflower 3,048  100.0(100.0) 2,936.2  100.0 (100.0)</p>
<p> Sorghum     802  100.0(100.0)   674.2   99.0  (99.2)</p>
<p> Cotton	956  100.0  (n/a)   810.3   91.4  (86.2)</p>
<p>((--Jason Webb, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655))</p>
